+# Agent Orchestrator runbook (PoC)
+
+Overview
+- The orchestrator accepts "plans" with ordered steps. Each step executes a tool in an isolated sandbox runner.
+- Evidence (plan, per-step results) is written to S3 under `agents/evidence/<plan_id>/`.
+
+Deployment notes
+- Deploy Redis and the orchestrator worker (services/agents/orchestrator_worker.py) as a Deployment with multiple replicas.
+- Deploy the sandbox runner as a separate service (ideally microVM-backed). Example runner stub is provided (services/sandbox/runner_stub.py) for testing only.
+- Ensure EVIDENCE_BUCKET is set for S3 evidence uploads.
+- Ensure SANDBOX_RUNNER_URL points to the sandbox runner service.
+- Enforce admission rules for sandbox & runner pods using RuntimeClass and admission webhook.
+
+Security
+- Replace the runner stub with a microVM-based runner (e.g., Firecracker/Kata) before running untrusted third-party tools.
+- Enforce per-run CPU/memory limits and timeouts. Record audit logs for each execution.
